From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:44:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Verifier V26: replay the lot's order bookkeeping from
 its history

V26:custody-history now also replays what a lot's own fields record of
its orders, between two recorded states:
- a new order's id lies in [old NONCE, new NONCE) and there are no more
  new orders than NONCE moved (set_order gives id NONCE, then moves it);
- with no order set in between (NONCE unchanged), CONSUMED grew by no
  more than the use orders already there gave up (only a use order's
  grantee consumes; returns only lower CONSUMED).
A break is a FAIL (CustodyHistoryBroken). IN_TOTAL grown beyond what the
caravans settled since could deliver is UNVERIFIABLE
(CustodyHistoryUnexplained), not a FAIL: a caravan may have been begun
and settled between two records. Instructions are still not replayed,
so a custody season is never a PASS.

tests/custody_history.rs: three forged bookkeepings fail; unexplained
goods in are unverifiable and not a fail; 9,000 windows of 1-4 composed
kernel steps never fail (184 are unexplained, as begun and settled
inside one window). Mutations of the three rules are caught.

